ng  from the narrative discourse to start I  think I'm in a good position to make  this video for one I obviously have a  pedigree of investment and appreciation  from software's approach to storytelling  I have a dark souls 3 video all about  how the placement of just one item tells  a story and provides context for the  area and the world a really good piece  of environmental storytelling that from  software is really big on in their  Narrative Approach and I have an Elden  ring video all about the themes of  struggle and perseverance that the game  really emphasizes both in story and in  gameplay reifying that story so I am one  who can see the Merit in the narrative  aspects of the game but at the same time  I think I may fall into a different boat  than a lot of the other Elden ring  creators defending the game obviously  they have a similar appreciation for the  game's storytelling but I think from  what I've seen that they haven't been  adequately responding to the issues  people have with the nomination I  basically think that they're giving  Eldon ring too much credit when it  should be criticized or at least  acknowledged to have a pretty mediocre  at best active story or plot and not to  say that there aren't toxic people  claiming Eldon ring has no narrative  Merit they are obviously wrong but so  too are Elden ring stands that are  deriding other games unconstructively  saying things like a cutscene fueled  story which is the traditional way of  Storytelling in video games is basically  more of a movie than a game I didn't  know we were saying Metal Gear games  aren't games anymore so the game awards  defines the criteria for the best  narrative award as the following for  outstanding storytelling and narrative  development in a game people are upset  that Elden ring is in the running versus  a game like God of War Ragnarok which  has much more clearer straightforward  storytelling and narrative development  now I actually think Eldon ring has  fantastic storytelling but its narrative  development like most from software  games is pretty mediocre in my opinion  we could bicker a bit about what  narrative development means and argue  Elden Rings cryptic piecemeal  storytelling counts as a form of  narrative but I think we'll have a  better discussion if we can agree to  just talk about the main present  narrative or story of the game basically  this would exclude the storytelling  found in Elden Ring's lore which anybody  watching my channel will probably agree  is done really well but that's not what  I think the core issue is in this  discussion many players go through Elden  ring or the soul series not really  knowing what they're doing plot wise the  same isn't true for God of War whatever  that discrepancy is is what I want to  talk about in this video  there is plenty to piece together in  Elden ring there are complex factions  and characters with buried motivations  that you can learn intimate details  about but in my experience that is  almost wholly confined to the lore the  actual story or Narrative of the game as  you play it the story of your tarnished  is a lacking one yes your character is a  blank slate to allow for character RPG  expression but the game doesn't let you  express that outside of your combat  playstyle your interactions with NPCs or  even lots of the world is not impacted  at all and this leads the game's story  progression to be pretty Hollow you are  simply that which kills the big bads and  maybe occasionally helps out an NPC with  their one Quest compare this to another  blank slate RPG IP The Fallout Series  where you have the same blank slate but  your RPG Investments and choices impact  your relationships with NPCs the kind of  person you are and how you can Traverse  the world the story elements are  adaptive to your role playing and there  are still substantive narrative  developments I also take issue with the  games and PCs many of these characters  have developed backstories like Ronnie  like and EG but their presence as  characters with significant development  or arcs is Bare Bones and lacking in the  present game as you play through it like  what is the character development of  Ronnie through the game or even Melina  do they change that much throughout the  Story from beginning to end do you see  their progression Melina and even  torrent would have been great cases to  have been more involved and had more  progression as characters since they are  always by our sides we could see them  grow and change and develop as we grow  through the world there is a tiny bit of  this with Melina disappearing coming  back and talking about her Newfound  resolve but that basically just puts her  in the same position as she was at the  start of the game yes there is some lore  contextual development but the actual  experience of the character in the story  is basically the same that progression  for either of them and a lot of the rest  of the cast simply isn't there and yeah  there are some cases of change like with  Bach or Eureka but these again are just  not that much box progression and  complexity as a character pale in  comparison to a lot of the characters in  God of War like freyas most of the main  characters in God of War feel much more  deeply developed by the game than those  in Eldon ring and that really isn't that  surprising when there's a lot more time  spent with them and they have a lot more  instances of dialogue there's roderica  who is a reference to farnes in berserk  but farnese has a hugely more developed  character Arc sure berserks a  decades-old manga but I'm just trying to  make the point that if we judge The  Narrative of Elden ring fairly not  handicapping it at all because it's just  a video game holding it to the same  standard as we would any other work of  art I think the active Narrative of  Alden ring is lacking the game world as  I play through it that's the important  part does not have very complex  developing characters nor a very  compelling plot like hayata has a cool  story and Quest but it really just isn't  that developed there isn't enough there  or time spent with her or interactions  or dialogue or actions on her part they  make for a developed character like we  see in any other kind of medium if we  saw hayata's story in another medium I  don't think she would come across as a  very developed or interesting character  because there isn't enough there I think  that's the case for a lot of people  myself often included for Elden ring now  of course the game does have some  narrative beats you find your maiden  dead you team up with Melina you get to  the Earth tree get rejected burn it all  down and defeat the boss Gauntlet at the  end but these don't feel like a fleshed  out story or Journey for the player  there isn't a ton of narrative  development going on throughout now this  is obviously kind of the point with the  style of game fromsoft is making insert  quote everybody's heard about Miyazaki  reading English novels as a kid not  understanding part of it and wanting to  make us feel the same way playing these  games  sekiro did not have these same story  issues to such a degree but it also had  a lack of the kind of lore so many  people myself included really love an  Eldon ring and other similar titles  overall I don't think this design  approach is worse though I do think the  game would benefit from a stronger more  developed story and more dynamic  characters after all those novels  miyazakirad had fully developed stories  and characters we always come to the  characters and bosses in these games  almost as relics we read of their past  accomplishments and Feats but the story  almost always feels basically over by  the time we arrive again I get that this  is partially the point but a little bit  of Leaning into allowing the player to  be more a part of that story just  sometimes would be something I would  find enjoyable basically if we the  players are like Miyazaki reading those  English novels give us just a little bit  better understanding of the language  instead of being an A1 or an A2 speaker  maybe sometimes let us be a B1 or a B2  speaker I don't want Elden ring or  future from software titles to be just  like other mainstream releases with all  the plainly straightforward narratives I  appreciate the difference in difficulty  storytelling approach and overall game  experience but at the same time that  doesn't mean I have to avoid all  criticism especially of something that  might seem core to that approach I think  Elden Ring's story is pretty lackluster  but I don't think that it has to be to  keep most or even all of the core  features that demarcate the game as a  special experience it's easy to say that  the game has a problem with boss reuse  but it's harder to genuinely say it has  a problem with narrative especially  because there are so many others saying  that who simply don't enjoy the overall  game philosophy and are just using this  as an excuse to attack the game I don't  want to change that philosophy I just  want a better story and those two things  are not mutually exclusive all that said  I am happy with the nomination at the  game awards I think Elden ring showcases  fantastic storytelling does mostly for  stuff that happened before we start  playing in the game world we do get to  experience the learning of that  information as players so it is very  much still in-game storytelling just of  a different kind and another YouTuber  the lore Hunter actually has a great  video just released on the idea of  finding the information and story as the  player you should really go check it out  if any of this video has been  interesting at all so I'm excited to see  what people think and how Elven ring and  God of War do at the awards in total I  haven't beaten God of War but from what  I've played I think Elden ring is still  the better game in my opinion I know  quite a surprise coming from the Elden  ring YouTuber God of War is fun but I  don't think it does enough with its  gameplay and it really seems to segment  gameplay and story as two separate  things which is not something I super  like have cutscenes sure but some of the  segments just seem to go a bit far from  me I may be streaming the game awards if  I can get my Internet to play nice but  either way I will be making a video if a  DLC announcement comes out I hope you  have enjoyed this video and if you have  any thoughts on the subject please leave  them in the comments I don't think I'll  have another video out before  Thanksgiving so Happy Thanksgiving to  everyone and if you don't celebrate that  specific holiday I wish you a happy  Happy fall harvest season and  celebration of some sort thanks so much  for watching feel free to join my  Discord in the description below and  I'll see you in the next video peace

